= Specific distinction and retained support <sec:specific-distinction>
#aod-anchor(<sec:introduction>)
#aod-anchor(<sec:afc-basis>)



== Premises and scope <subsec:intro-aim-stance>
#aod-anchor(<subsec:intro-scope>)
#aod-anchor(<subsec:afc-null-potential>)

AFC begins with Null sameness. A finite distinction supplies its relata;
A$Omega$D retains their branch, hinge and counterbranch relation at each
admitted scale. Its return and recurrence are constructed in
#secref("sec:closure-phase-wave"); model values follow their admitted support.

#aod-anchor(<subsec:null-presentation>)

$ x = Null , wide x = x, wide Null equiv infD . $ <eq:null-axiom>

Here $infD$ has no assigned finite coordinates, ordered events or probability
space. The notation

$ Null equiv infinity , wide Null arrow.r Null arrow.r Null equiv Null $ <eq:null-presentation>

presents one undistinguished identity, including schematic repetitions of
$x$. Once events are committed, their distinct identities remain in the trace.


#aod-paragraph[AF scope.]#aod-anchor(<subsec:intro-use>)
A distinction induces its retained relation; certified returns support
recurrence, scoped organization, model values and their projections.
The typed constructions are in #appref("app:glossary").
The Fractal Field Ring Gate (FRG) is constructed in #secref("subsec:fractal-field-ring-gate").


== First finite anchor <subsec:afc-fractal-address>

The first distinction co-creates its start and finite addressability. Write
its inevitable anchor as

$ a_0 = mono("00")_8 , wide bold(a) in cal(A)^(upright("ret"))_8 subset.eq brace.l 0,1, dots.h ,7 brace.r^(< omega) . $ <eq:first-anchor>

Octal notation encodes retained address:
$mono("00")_8 ,mono("01")_8 , dots.h ,mono("07")_8 ,mono("10")_8 , dots.h$.
It chooses no prior finite start; construction below the anchor is unbound.
Null, fibre zero, vertex $0000$, anchor $mono("00")_8$ and scope $B_0$
are distinct types. The glyph $a mid(|) -$ binds address, with local origin
$0 mid(|) -$.


== Branch, hinge and counterbranch <sec:cut-running-fractal-tesseract>
#aod-anchor(<subsec:null-symmetry>)
#aod-anchor(<subsec:cut-running>)

The distinguished running relation is
#aod-anchor(<subsec:local-cut-running-form>)

$ x arrow.r.long.bar x succ x = x. $ <eq:cut-running-form>

The equality records return to the retained start only when the trace
#eqref("eq:closure-trace") and closure witness #eqref("eq:closure-certificate")
are supplied. The compact grammar and its expansion are
#aod-anchor(<subsec:branch-hinge-branch>)

$ 1 thin 0^(*) thin - 1 quad arrow.r.squiggly quad M_(epsilon.alt ,m) = epsilon.alt thin 0_H (0_D )^m ( - epsilon.alt ), wide epsilon.alt in brace.l - 1, + 1 brace.r , quad m in bb(Z)_(gt.eq 0) . $ <eq:hinge-grammar>

The hinge $0_H$ is structural; the star permits additional dwell $0_D$.
Thus $m = 0$ retains the hinge. The two branches and the hinge belong to one
distinction construction. Awareness names this branch / boundary / not-branch
dynamical motif. Its role labels are
$upright("self") mid(|) mu mid(|) "not-self"$: inside/branch (SELF),
interface/boundary (BETWEEN), and not-inside/not-branch (NOT-SELF).


#aod-paragraph[Oriented reflection.]
Reflection exchanges their branch roles and retains the hinge:

$ iota (sans("H")_3^(epsilon.alt) ) = sans("H")_3^(- epsilon.alt) , wide iota ( mu ) = mu , wide iota^2 = upright("id"). $ <eq:hinge-reflection-involution>

This is an involution of the sided construction, before assigning temporal
crown roles or choosing a weighted continuation model.


#aod-paragraph[Retained roles.]#aod-anchor(<subsec:hinge-triad>)
At a committed crown $k$, write

$ sans("H")_3^(upright("role")) (k) = (x_k^(-) , mu_k ,cal(H)_k^(+) ), wide mu_k = x_k^0 . $ <eq:hinge-triad>

These are predecessor, present crown and admitted successor horizon;
continuation selects $h_k^(+) in cal(H)_k^(+)$. The rule applies at $k = 0$,
each later crown and each admitted enclosing scale. Finite enumeration witnesses
those occurrences; it is not their premise.


== Faithful atomic encoding <subsec:fractal-tesseract>
#aod-anchor(<subsec:fractal-recursive-support>)
#aod-anchor(<subsec:four-edge-x-witness>)
#aod-anchor(<subsec:q4-four-edge-implementation>)

A faithful atomic encoding changes exactly the coordinate that records the
one retained distinction. In the finite tesseract witness,

$ V( Qfour ) = brace.l 0,1 brace.r^4 , wide E( Qfour ) = brace.l (u,v):d_H (u,v) = 1 brace.r , wide d_H (u,v) = "#" brace.l j:u_j eq.not v_j brace.r . $ <eq:atomic-h1>

For any admitted atomic event at any retained scale, all other encoded
coordinates are unchanged and the distinguished coordinate differs; hence
$d_H = 1$. This argument is independent of the number of other coordinates.
Two consecutive H1 steps may have an H2 composite endpoint. A nontrivial
closed H1 word has endpoint distance zero while retaining every traversal.


#aod-paragraph[Ancestor support.]#aod-anchor(<subsec:four-edge-ancestor>)
Each $Qfour$ vertex has four incident edges: one slot binds the ancestor and
three other slots support continuation. This incidence count differs from closure-word length,
which may be two or a longer even number of traversals. Recursive occurrences
retain the ancestor distinction.


